REQUIREMENTS

This software requires certain third-party components under open-source
licenses to be built and executed. These components are not included in or
distributed with this software: they are downloaded automatically from their
public registries (npm registry, Docker Hub) when the software is built, in one
of the following two ways.

- With Docker (recommended): the user only needs Docker Engine with Docker
  Compose. "docker compose up --build" pulls the Node.js and MongoDB images
  and runs "npm ci" inside the images, which downloads the npm packages listed
  below and their dependencies.
- Manual installation: the user needs Node.js, MongoDB and git installed.
  Running "npm install" in webgme-app and mcp-server downloads the npm packages
  listed below and their dependencies (git is used by bower to fetch the
  client libraries of webgme-codeeditor).

The npm packages listed below are the direct dependencies of each part; npm
also downloads their transitive dependencies, each under its own license.
This information is provided solely for transparency and traceability purposes.
It does not modify, replace, or extend the license terms applicable to each
third-party component. The versions are those resolved in the package-lock.json
files of this release.

